{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01UM7yj2EW7GMnn6Qv5UmcXn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## rnd-v11.1 â€” \"Handoff Always Primes\" â€” Session Summary\n\n**Goal:** Close the v11 keystone's last gap â€” a research session whose work existed *only* as a terminal conversation (no written file) used to refuse the advance (\"no materials\") or open the next stage with a misleading bare prompt. v11.1 makes the handoff always prime the next stage. Built by Foreman on branch `foreman/rnd-surface-v11.1` (off master `b6719bd`, v11 merged), 3 waves, all GREEN.\n\n### Grounded claims\n\n- **Wave 1 (keystone, backend) â€” GREEN after 3 iters, ending GREEN 1254.** `prepare_stage_handoff` gained a synchronous transcript snapshot: when the initial persist yields no doc-classified file, it reads the source PTY buffer (`read_since(sid,0)`), cleans it, writes `<source_worktree>/<lane>/<sid[:12]>-transcript.md`, re-persists it (session-tagged), and builds the real doc-referencing prompt. Best-effort, never-raises, fires only in the no-doc case. `handoff.build_next_stage_prompt`'s no-docs fallback was rewritten honest + actionable (\"create the materials\"), never claiming a non-existent report.\n\n- **Wave 1 review caught a real stub-blind-spot (NO-GO â†’ fixed).** First green proved plumbing but not value: the cleaner's `\\r`-replace *expanded* spinner redraws and the byte-exact seed-strip failed on wrapped output, so on real ConPTY the transcript would be dominated by redraw chrome with the Q&A buried â€” the exact stub-blindness v11 was meant to kill. **FIX iter 1:** rewrote `_clean_transcript_text` into a 6-stage real-ConPTY pipeline (redraw frame-collapse â†’ broadened ANSI/CSI/OSC/DCS strip â†’ wrap-tolerant seed/greet strip â†’ chrome drop â†’ dup-line collapse â†’ HEAD+TAIL cap).\n\n- **Wave 1 also fixed a dead prod path + a regression it introduced.** The background-refine was gated on `ANCHOR_PROACTIVE_SUMMARY`, which `main()` never exported (only the module flag was set) â€” so `anchor_gui.main()` now exports `ANCHOR_PROACTIVE_SUMMARY=1`. Making the gate live exposed a prod double-summary (kill fires the finish hook *and* the keystone background summary for the same session); **FIX iter 2** made `_trigger_background_source_summary` skip a TERMINAL source (finish hook owns it) while still firing for a LIVE source.\n\n- **Wave 2 (grass, UI) â€” GREEN after 2 iters, ending GREEN 1260; John signed off 2026-06-20.** Removed the `no-research-material` hard-refusal in `advance_grass_research_to_plan` so grass falls through to the v10 W5 contained-grass mint/focus/link machinery with the transcript-backed (or honest-minimal) prompt â€” grass now always opens the plan session like the non-grass path. The `no-research-session` negative (nothing to advance from) was kept.\n\n- **Wave 2 review caught a silent broken-handoff ordering bug (BLOCKER â†’ fixed).** Develop-plan-first + conversation-only: the transcript was committed to main HEAD and named in the prompt, but the pre-existing plan worktree was cut *before* the commit, so the file was absent from its checkout (Crucible would hit file-not-found). **FIX:** `_materialize_handoff_into_plan_worktree` copies the persisted transcript/doc rels from the main folder into the plan worktree and writes HANDOFF.md + NEXT-PROMPT.md there (matching the non-grass path), wired into both fresh-mint and focused-existing branches; a new test asserts the file is actually on disk (proven to fail pre-fix).\n\n- **Wave 3 (healthcheck + docs) â€” GREEN 1266, PROJECT DONE.** `anchor_healthcheck.check_rnd_v11_1_surface` (registered in `main()`) walks the real conversation-only flow fully stubbed â€” seeding the stub PTY *buffer* (no file/`record_effort`/kill) for both researchâ†’plan and grass, asserting the transcript is snapshotted, persisted, committed, named in the prompt, materialized on disk in the plan worktree, contained, linked, and idempotent. `ANCHOR_PROACTIVE_SUMMARY` is saved/restored in an unconditional `finally` (load-bearing since the keystone now reads that env). CLAUDE.md v11.1 section added; distro scan clean (no new modules).\n\n- **Verification discipline / lesson.** A conversation-only test must seed the stub PTY read buffer (not write a file) â€” a pre-written-file test is prompt-building coverage; a pre-persisted-effort test is the v11 masking trap; neither exercises the conversation-only path that broke in production.\n\n- **Status:** All 3 waves GREEN (1266 passed, 1 skipped). Branch ready but **not merged / not deployed** â€” no merge or `nssm restart` until John signs off the whole branch (Wave 2's individual sign-off is recorded, but final branch merge is pending)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":638,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3701,"cache_read_input_tokens":88286,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3701},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2071fb97-0a13-4312-a389-5e11c936836f","uuid":"45d6adcd-47bf-4c42-bd8e-e2b8710f1f68","request_id":"req_011CcFpHpo3d81XPmomfR6YM"}
